# Empty and error states

An empty screen is a message. First use, no matches, no access and a failed load
each mean something different, so each needs its own words and its own next
step. Compose [EmptyState](squonk-ui://components/empty-state) with a
[Button](squonk-ui://components/button) or [Link](squonk-ui://components/link).

**Example:** First use, no matches and a failed load. “Create”, “Clear search” and “Try again” are not interchangeable.

```tsx
export function EmptyStatesExample() {
  return (
    <Grid columns={{ mobile: 1, tablet: 3 }} gap="md">
      <Card variant="outlined">
        <EmptyState title="No sightings yet" body="Sightings you log appear here." action={<Button variant="primary">Log a sighting</Button>} />
      </Card>
      <Card variant="outlined">
        <EmptyState icon={<SearchIcon />} title="No matches for 'hemlock'" body="Check the spelling or search for something else." action={<Button variant="secondary">Clear search</Button>} />
      </Card>
      <Card variant="outlined">
        <EmptyState icon={<ErrorIcon />} title="We couldn't load your sightings" body="Your sightings are safe. Try again in a moment." action={<Button variant="secondary">Try again</Button>} />
      </Card>
    </Grid>
  );
}

/** A failed load, said plainly, with a retry. */
```

## The rules

- **Say what happened, then the next useful step.** Keep the title short.
- **Never show a failed load as “nothing here”.** It tells people their records
  are gone.
- **Keep what's already on screen during a refresh.** Show the empty state only
  once you know there's nothing.
- **Fit the space.** In a small card or table, drop the icon and use one action.
  Pass it to [Table](squonk-ui://components/table) as `empty`.

**Do:** The load failed, so it says so and offers to try again.

```tsx
export function FailedLoadExample() {
  return (
    <Card variant="outlined">
      <EmptyState icon={<ErrorIcon />} title="We couldn't load your sightings" body="Your sightings are safe. Try again in a moment." action={<Button variant="secondary">Try again</Button>} />
    </Card>
  );
}

/** A failed load presented as "nothing here". */
```

**Don't:** The same failure shown as first use: people think their sightings have gone.

```tsx
export function MisleadingEmptyExample() {
  return (
    <Card variant="outlined">
      <EmptyState title="No sightings yet" body="Sightings you log appear here." action={<Button variant="primary">Log a sighting</Button>} />
    </Card>
  );
}

